From cab92f8a226b02a5820a1287fd0cf46fa0b94557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:53:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/51] B70-IP-K6: --kv-cache-dtype int8_per_token_head for
 Qwen4Exp QSA

What: the QSA backend, impl and owner accept int8_per_token_head. The backend
packs the spec like TRITON_ATTN (customize_spec: K | f32 | V | f32 per cell,
520 B at head_dim 256), and so does QSAStateBackend for a main-attention
per-token-head spec: the indexer's state caches register before their owner,
so the platform's hybrid block alignment asks that backend for the main
per-token page. The impl keeps cached scale views (dropped by the runner's
post-profiling reset like TRITON_ATTN's), writes through the fused prepare
(main_kv_pth) or, unfused, through the Triton per-token-head writer (K/V cut
to slot_mapping), and hands the views to the QSA kernels. The warmup passes
head_dim. One info line names the int8 path.

Why: QFN INT8 KV vs FP8 KV, side by side. The drafter (TRITON_ATTN) already
handles the dtype; its pages share the inline layout, so B70-IP-K3's unify
sees commensurate pages.

bf16/fp8: customize_spec returns those specs unchanged; every other change is
behind the int8 dtype.

Measured: CPU tests only (next commit). Boot and serving not run.
